---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import TimeLineElement from "../components/cv/TimeLine.astro";
import { getBaseUrl } from "../lib/getBaseUrl";

const base = getBaseUrl();
---

<BaseLayout
  title="John Dorion - Professional Resume & Experience"
  description="Security practitioner and consulting engineer working across detection engineering, security operations, identity, and cloud infrastructure. Splunk Enterprise Security Certified Admin, AWS Solutions Architect Associate, two-time CTF winner, and homelab builder."
  showTranslateButton={true}
>
  <div class="mb-5">
    <h1 class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">John's Resume</h1>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10 text-justify">
    I'm currently a Consulting Engineer at Silex Data Solutions, helping clients make sense of complex
    infrastructure, cloud, and security problems. Before that I spent a couple of years in security operations:
    building Splunk and CrowdStrike detections for a large enterprise security team and then supervising the analysts
    working that queue, and before that running an L1/L2 access queue and reviewing vendor controls.
    I also run a homelab where I've picked up most of my Linux, virtualization, and networking knowledge. When I'm
    not working, you might find me competing in CTF competitions or tinkering with my Proxmox cluster.
  </div>

  <!-- Key Achievements -->
  <div class="mb-5">
    <h2 class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Key Achievements</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-10">
    <div class="flip-card">
      <span class="sr-only">Tech 901 CTF - Press Enter or Space to flip card</span>
      <div class="flip-card-inner">
        <div class="flip-card-front card bg-base-200 shadow-xl">
          <div class="card-body items-center justify-center text-center p-6">
            <div class="text-4xl">🏆</div>
            <h3 class="card-title text-sm mt-2">Tech 901 CTF</h3>
            <p class="text-primary font-bold">1st Place 2024 & 2025</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flip-card-back shadow-xl rounded-2xl">
          <p>Back-to-back winner of Memphis Tech 901's annual capture-the-flag competition. Competitor in other CTFs</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="flip-card">
      <span class="sr-only">Professional Credentials - Press Enter or Space to flip card</span>
      <div class="flip-card-inner">
        <div class="flip-card-front card bg-base-200 shadow-xl">
          <div class="card-body items-center justify-center text-center p-6">
            <div class="text-4xl">📜</div>
            <h3 class="card-title text-sm mt-2">Professional Credentials</h3>
            <p class="text-primary font-bold">30+ Certifications</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flip-card-back shadow-xl rounded-2xl">
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-left">
            <li>Splunk ES Certified Admin</li>
            <li>Splunk Cybersecurity Defense Analyst</li>
            <li>AWS Solutions Architect Associate</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="flip-card">
      <span class="sr-only">I learn by building - Press Enter or Space to flip card</span>
      <div class="flip-card-inner">
        <div class="flip-card-front card bg-base-200 shadow-xl">
          <div class="card-body items-center justify-center text-center p-6">
            <div class="text-4xl">🛠️</div>
            <h3 class="card-title text-sm mt-2">I learn by</h3>
            <p class="text-primary font-bold">Building!</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flip-card-back shadow-xl rounded-2xl">
          <p>Self-taught infrastructure: Splunk, Proxmox, OPNsense, Ansible, NixOS.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <h2 class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Education</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container grid gap-4 mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Graduate Certificate in Business Project Management"
      subtitle="2024 - 2025 at Fogelman College of Business & Economics, University of Memphis"
      accent={true}
    />
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Bachelor of Business Administration - Business Information Technology"
      subtitle="2023 - 2024 at Fogelman College of Business & Economics, University of Memphis | GPA: 3.8"
    >
      <p class="ml-4">Magna Cum Laude, Dean's List. Organization: MILE Leadership Program</p>
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Associate of Science - Business Administration"
      subtitle="Southwest Tennessee Community College"
    >
      <p class="ml-4">Magna Cum Laude</p>
    </TimeLineElement>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <h2 class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Experience</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container mb-10 space-y-6">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Associate Consulting Engineer / Sales Engineer"
      subtitle="Dec 2024 - Present at Silex Data Solutions, Memphis, TN"
      accent={true}
    >
      <ul class="list-disc ml-4 space-y-1">
        <li>Run technical discovery with customer application, infrastructure, and security teams to understand their environment, what they are trying to accomplish, and what stands in the way, then scope the work that follows</li>
        <li>Manage several client engagements at once across security analytics, cloud, and infrastructure, tracking dependencies, decisions, and blockers through delivery and handoff</li>
        <li>Research emerging data protection problems, including the data loss risk created by generative AI tools and where conventional DLP coverage breaks down against prompts, uploads, and integrations</li>
        <li>Maintain technical credibility through continuous certification in AWS, Splunk, Red Hat, Zscaler, and other enterprise platforms</li>
      </ul>
    </TimeLineElement>

    <TimeLineElement
      title="Vice President & Operations Lead"
      subtitle="Jan 2026 - Present at BSides Memphis (Volunteer, Part-Time)"
      url="https://bsidesmemphis.org"
      accent={true}
    >
      <ul class="list-disc ml-4 space-y-1">
        <li>Administer the organization Google Workspace tenant: user and group lifecycle, access control, sharing settings, DNS, and SPF, DKIM, and DMARC</li>
        <li>Coordinate conference operations across vendor and venue relationships and the budget with a committee of volunteers</li>
      </ul>
    </TimeLineElement>

    <TimeLineElement
      title="InfoSec Technical Supervisor & Project Coordinator"
      subtitle="Apr 2024 - Dec 2024 at UMRF Ventures, Memphis, TN"
    >
      <ul class="list-disc ml-4 space-y-1">
        <li>Supervised an analyst team investigating and tuning Splunk and CrowdStrike alerts for an enterprise security operations group, owning what got worked, what got escalated, and what got closed</li>
        <li>Built CrowdStrike alerts to detect data exfiltration based on file type and device type, covering sensitive files moving to removable media and other unmanaged devices</li>
        <li>Consolidated team knowledge into SharePoint and streamlined it into a single source of truth</li>
        <li>Put change control around detection content with source control, peer review, and testing before anything reached production</li>
        <li>Directed development of Python tooling on Google Cloud Platform that pulled from REST APIs and applied machine learning to security log analysis, surfacing activity that rule-based logic missed</li>
        <li>Reported alert volume, coverage gaps, and delivery metrics to client leadership, and presented findings to business and executive stakeholders outside the security organization</li>
      </ul>
    </TimeLineElement>

    <TimeLineElement
      title="InfoSec Data Scientist / Detection Developer"
      subtitle="Dec 2023 - Apr 2024 at UMRF Ventures, Memphis, TN"
    >
      <ul class="list-disc ml-4 space-y-1">
        <li>Built and tuned Splunk Cloud dashboards, alerts, and scheduled searches using SPL across enterprise log sources, applying performance-conscious search design to large data volumes</li>
        <li>Translated MITRE ATT&CK techniques and independent research into tested detection logic, adjusting thresholds with stakeholders to cut false positives</li>
        <li>Normalized and enriched event data against the Splunk Common Information Model using field aliases, calculated fields, tags, event types, and lookups to enable correlation across disparate sources</li>
        <li>Validated onboarded log sources for timestamp accuracy, sourcetype assignment, event breaking, and field extraction, and identified sensitive information in ingested data that was escalated to security leadership for remediation</li>
      </ul>
    </TimeLineElement>

    <TimeLineElement
